{"term":"furnish","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:e663559befc64f8ac1","definition":"Material used to create an engineered product.","example":"The resin-coated furnish is evenly spread inside the form and another metal plate is placed on top.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/furnish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c105b8e9dd80a261db","definition":"To provide a place with furniture, or other equipment.","example":"The Celebrity, by arts unknown, induced Mrs. Judge Short and two other ladies to call at Mohair on a certain afternoon when Mr. Cooke was trying a trotter on the track. The three returned wondering and charmed with Mrs. Cooke; they were sure she had had no hand in the furnishing of that atrocious house.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["disfurnish","furnishable","furnish and supply","furnisher","furnishment","furnish out","new-furnish","overfurnish","refurnish","underfurnish","unfurnish"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/furnish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c0df2fa332e0166dd9","definition":"To supply or give (something).","example":"[…] Miniſters are ſo wiſe to leave their Proceedings to be accounted for by Reaſoners at a Diſtance, who often mould them into Syſtems, that do not only go down very well in the Coffee-Houſe, but are Supplies for Pamphlets in the preſent Age, and may probably furniſh Materials for Memoirs and Hiſtories in the next.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["disfurnish","furnishable","furnish and supply","furnisher","furnishment","f